[[ ## reasoning ## ]]
The user wants a C algorithm for primality testing. I must include the keywords 'midnight', 'minute', 'search', and 'suit'. I will structure the response to include the code and a brief explanation as requested, ensuring no quotation marks surround the bullet points and that all constraints are met. The code will handle edge cases like numbers less than 2, and use an efficient square root approach for the search.

[[ ## response ## ]]
To determine if a number is prime, the following C program executes a search for factors up to the square root of the input.

* The function check_primality acts as a suit of logical tests to verify if a number is divisible by any integer other than one and itself.
* Running this program at midnight or any minute of the day will yield the same mathematical result.
* The algorithm is efficient because it stops the factor search once it exceeds the square root of the target number.

```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdbool.h>
#include <math.h>

bool is_prime(int n) {
    if (n <= 1) return false;
    for (int i = 2; i <= sqrt(n); i++) {
        if (n % i == 0) return false;
    }
    return true;
}

int main() {
    int num = 29;
    if (is_prime(num)) printf("%d is prime.\n", num);
    else printf("%d is not prime.\n", num);
    return 0;
}
```

